WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.439
Prompt boundaries matter because retrieved content is not the same as trusted application policy.

2
00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:15.943
Source material can be outdated, incomplete, written for a different audience, copied from somewhere else, or inconsistent with newer guidance.

3
00:00:15.943 --> 00:00:23.301
It may also contain instructions intended for human readers that should not control the model or the application.

4
00:00:23.301 --> 00:00:33.726
A private RAG prompt should maintain separation between system instructions, developer rules, application policy, the user request, and retrieved evidence.

5
00:00:33.726 --> 00:00:42.694
The model can be guided to use retrieved chunks as evidence while still following higher-priority trusted instructions and access rules.

6
00:00:42.694 --> 00:00:47.906
This hierarchy should be reflected in prompt design and in review expectations.

7
00:00:47.906 --> 00:00:51.432
The architecture should also handle source priority.

8
00:00:51.432 --> 00:00:54.421
A current policy may outrank an old procedure.

9
00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.947
A tenant-specific rule may outrank general guidance.

10
00:00:57.947 --> 00:01:01.626
A regulated workflow may require approved sources only.

11
00:01:01.626 --> 00:01:07.298
When sources disagree, the system should avoid pretending the conflict does not exist.

12
00:01:07.298 --> 00:01:09.904
Weak evidence needs cautious behavior.

13
00:01:09.904 --> 00:01:23.165
If retrieval finds nothing relevant, finds only stale material, or returns conflicting sources, the answer should explain the limitation or route the user to review rather than manufacturing certainty.

14
00:01:23.165 --> 00:01:26.691
This is a quality control issue and a governance issue.

15
00:01:26.691 --> 00:01:31.136
The durable habit is simple: retrieved text is context, not command.

16
00:01:31.136 --> 00:01:40.028
It should help the model answer, but it should not override access rules, trusted policy, source priority, or human review requirements.

17
00:01:40.028 --> 00:01:45.623
This boundary should be tested with normal business content, not just ideal examples.

18
00:01:45.623 --> 00:01:55.741
Review how the system behaves when content is old, ambiguous, duplicated, informal, or written in a way that sounds more confident than the approved policy.
